From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:20:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AOT: variables narrowed in loops, closure variables
 written before they are read, integer remainders, methods of a few functions

- In the fast copy of a loop, a read of a module or closure variable that is
  written with nothing but numbers, strings, booleans, arrays or typed arrays
  is taken for what is written, behind a check that leaves for the generic
  copy (useAOTVariableNarrowing). Before, the undefined or hole a variable
  starts as made `i < N` with a module constant N a generic compare: 8x.
  A loop that reads such a variable gets a fast copy where it would have
  been kept whole, unless it has a call made part of it.
- A read of a variable of an environment the function made, after a store
  to the same variable of the same environment, is of the written types
  (a constant captured by a closure made part of the function).
- `a % b` of numbers not proven integers: an integer remainder when both are
  int32s, the one not negative and not -0, the other positive; fmod
  otherwise (useAOTIntegerRemainderOfNumbers).
- In the fast copy of a loop, a method call whose name the program gives to
  2-6 functions (maximumAOTMethodCandidates, within a bytecode budget) is
  split into a check for each function in turn, each leading to a copy of
  the call known to be to that function and inlined; the last check leaves
  for the generic copy. The read of the method then goes through the stub,
  whose cache holds several structures.
- The method check also requires code in the image for a call: a function
  without it has index 0, the first function's.
- Graph::computeDominators(), from LoopOptimizer, for type inference too.
